From cab52663cf40d1668f0a8a367ab85df6cbb75568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: benbreen <8338320+benbreen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:12:24 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] kosmickrisp: reset the geometry heap exactly once per
 command buffer

Do not clear cmd->uses_heap in kk_cmd_buffer_dirty_all_gfx (it runs on
mid-command-buffer render pass restarts), so a second heap reset cannot
reallocate from offset 0 and overwrite indices an earlier draw has not yet
consumed (giant-triangle artifact). uses_heap is still cleared in
kk_reset_cmd_buffer_internal when the command buffer is recycled.

Ported to mesa-26.3.0-rc3. Only the uses_heap half carries over: rc3 (since
0126f4388a5, one MTL4CommandBuffer per VkCommandBuffer) encodes the heap
reset in-line with a barrier, so the original's pre_gfx-encoder ordering
hunk has no counterpart.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
index 46dfa33f6ec..543f9a0d0a3 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -315,10 +315,13 @@ kk_cmd_buffer_dirty_all_gfx(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
    cmd->state.gfx.dirty = ~0u;
    cmd->state.gfx.descriptors.root_dirty = true;
 
-   /* We just flushed out the heap use. If we want to use it again, we'll need
-    * to queue a free for it again.
-    */
-   cmd->uses_heap = false;
+   /* NOTE: do NOT clear cmd->uses_heap here. This runs on mid-command-buffer
+    * render pass restarts (e.g. around meta blits such as font-atlas uploads).
+    * Clearing it made kk_heap() encode a SECOND heap reset (bottom=0) into the
+    * same command buffer, so a later unroll could reallocate from offset 0 and
+    * overwrite indices an earlier draw had not consumed yet (giant-triangle
+    * artifact in BAR). The heap is reset once per command buffer execution;
+    * uses_heap is cleared when the command buffer is recycled. */
 }
 
 void kk_cmd_release_dynamic_ds_state(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
